course: dictionary
lesson: 8269
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. «Rig» is a good example: it can be an action word (a verb) or a thing (a noun). The words around it tell you which meaning the writer means.
explain: Look at the clues. «The other team was scripted to win!» Then someone asks «Rigged?» A rigged game is one where the result was fixed in secret, so to rig something means to arrange it dishonestly.
explain: Now read «Oisín's da works on an oil rig: two weeks away, two weeks home.» Here rig is a noun, a large structure out at sea for drilling for oil or gas. Ask yourself: does my meaning fit the sentence? If it does, you have found the right one.
fact: Rig can be a verb: to rig something means to arrange it dishonestly so a certain result happens, like rigging a vote.
fact: To rig up means to build or set something up quickly from whatever you have.
fact: On a boat, the rigging is the ropes and sails.
fact: An oil rig is a large structure for drilling for oil or gas, often standing in the sea.
fact: In some countries, a rig can be a large truck, or a set of equipment.
exercise: «The other team was scripted to win!» Why did someone say «Rigged?» | *The game was secretly fixed so one side would win | The players were tired and slow | The score was a draw | The game was played in the rain
exercise: «Oisín's da works on an oil rig: two weeks away, two weeks home.» Where does Oisín's da work? | In a school, teaching children | On a farm with cows | In a shop by the harbour | *Out at sea, on a large structure for drilling for oil
exercise: Mia needs a shelter for the school play, so she will rig up a tent from sticks and a tarp. What does rig up mean? | To sail a boat across the sea | To drill a hole deep in the ground | To cheat in a game | *To build or set something up quickly from what you have
test: The vote was rigged, so the result was decided before anyone voted. What does rigged mean here? | To change the rules for next year | *To arrange something dishonestly so a certain result happens | To hold a vote in the school hall | To count the votes very carefully
test: The sailors checked the rigging before they set off. What is the rigging? | The map of the sea | *The ropes and sails on a boat | The engine at the back of the boat | The shoes the sailors wear
exam: «The crew had to rig the boat before the storm.» What does rig mean in this sentence? | To sink the boat on purpose | *To fit the boat with ropes and sails | To sell the boat to a friend | To paint the boat bright red
